<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 21.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 21.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for March 21.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Mar    208.00    212.50    213.50     224.00</p>
<p>    Apr    206.00    210.50    211.50     224.00</p>
<p>    May    206.00    210.50    211.50     224.00</p>
<p>    Jun    201.50    206.00    207.00     223.00</p>
<p>    Jul    200.00    204.50    205.50     201.50</p>
<p>    Aug    199.00    203.50    204.50     200.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$2.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	176.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  151.50	    Port Adelaide	 153.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     151.75	    Port Giles	    153.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	149.50	    Wallaroo		151.50</p>
<p>    New South Wales			Port Pirie	    148.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     151.50	    Port Lincoln	  154.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   152.00	    Thevenard	     149.75</p>
<p>    Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 151.00	     Esperance	    156.25</p>
<p>    Portland	152.00	     Albany		 157.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    159.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    157.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
